      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Sorting</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Counting</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Sorting and counting</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Sorting is rarely the answer; it is the move that makes the answer easy. Learn when to sort first, how to write a comparator that never breaks, when counting beats comparing (O(n + k)), how merge sort counts pairs while it merges (reverse pairs, smaller-after-self), and how partitioning gives you the k-th element in expected O(n). Templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\n"
